    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting an elite 81.88 efficiency score. His matchup against R. V\u00e1squez (4.89 xERA) combined with a massive 16% park adjustment and 19% SP skill advantage makes him our most bankable asset. Close behind is **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who benefits from a highly favorable encounter with Gibson (5.87 xERA). Both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** are positioned to capitalize on poor opposing pitching, serving as the core anchors for our production targets today.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages are driving much of our middle-tier value. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.33) carries a strong 14% platoon boost against L. Castillo, effectively securing his spot in the lineup. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Nasim Nunez** (48.39) and **Wade Meckler** (41.07), who remain in the lineup despite lower scores to capture potential SB opportunities, though **Nasim Nunez** faces an efficiency drag due to his bottom-of-the-order placement. The most difficult bench decision was **Nolan Schanuel** (44.14); he narrowly missed the cut because the optimizer favored the higher platoon-adjusted ceilings of our outfield depth against weaker starters.\n\nRegarding risks, we must monitor the status of **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler**, both of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have projected them in the #5 and #3 spots respectively, any downward shift in the order could jeopardize their efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Sam Antonacci** projects as a start, his matchup against the elite Yamamoto (3.33 xERA) is a significant drag on his score (16% SP skill penalty); we are relying on his leadoff spot to offset the matchup difficulty. Finally, we continue to stash **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, awaiting his return to bolster our scarcity-driven SB strategy.",
